{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>האומן</b> — tagin on the heh, for five things a father merits for his sons, and they are: beauty, strength, wealth, wisdom, and years. Beauty, as stated: \"Your work to Your servants, and Your splendor upon their sons.\" Strength, as stated: \"His seed shall be mighty in the earth; the generation of the upright shall be blessed.\" Wealth, as stated: \"I was young and also grew old, and I have not seen a righteous one forsaken, nor his seed seeking bread; all the day he grants and lends, and his seed is for blessing.\" Wisdom, as stated: \"Instead of your fathers shall be your sons; you shall make them princes in all the earth,\" and it is written: \"They shall not depart from your mouth, nor from the mouth of your seed, nor from the mouth of your seed's seed.\" Years, as written: \"That your days may be multiplied, and the days of your sons, upon the land.\" And just as he merits these for them, so he obligates them in five things — their counterparts — as written: \"May they come upon the head of Joab and upon all his father's house, and may there not be cut off from the house of Joab one with a discharge, and a leper, and one who grasps the distaff, and one who falls by the sword, and one lacking bread.\" One with a discharge — in place of strength, for discharge drains the strength. A leper — in place of beauty, for leprosy is repulsive to people. One who grasps the distaff — a pit that has no wisdom. One who falls by the sword — short of days. One lacking bread — this is poverty, in place of wealth. Found: the righteous one merits for his sons five things, and the culpable one obligates his sons in five things — their counterparts:"], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The five tagin on the heh of האומן correspond to the five merits; each merit has a matching curse drawn from the Joab passage. The phrase 'בור שאין בו חכמה' (a pit with no wisdom) is a parenthetical gloss on 'מחזיק בפלך' as a type lacking wisdom."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:58.885916872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}